From 067bf735df1a2d1cfc549909c6846f5287b185c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-bot <lccc-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:45:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix decimal32-arm-width IVSR regression, add
 iv_widen/peephole tests, and drop load_op_fuse extraction

Cross-Target IVSR & AArch64 Indexed Store Folding
- Commit 3dbed46e2 enabled unconditional affine recognition for Shl in
  iv_strength_reduce::find_derived_exprs, which rewrote a[i + 1] ((i + 1) << 2)
  in tests/regression/decimal32_indexed_fold_arm.c into a constant-offset
  sibling GEP across bl __bid_addsd3 and broke the decimal32-arm-width CI gate
  (no folded str w0, [x23, x19, lsl #2]).
- Gate Shl find_affine on (shift > 3 || !gep_uses_by_index.contains_key(&dest.0))
  without consulting compare_recurrence::enabled(): non-GEP shifts and wide GEP
  shifts (shift > 3, stride >= 16) are recognized on every target, while
  hardware-scalable GEP shifts (shift <= 3, stride in {1, 2, 4, 8}) stay in
  indexed form so AArch64 ([xB, xI, lsl #1..3]) and x86 SIB fold them directly
  into the memory instruction.
- Add affine_shift_recognizes_scalar_and_wide_gep_while_preserving_sib_gep in
  iv_strength_reduce.rs.

Unit Tests for iv_widen, narrow_copy_fold, and relay_and_lea
- iv_widen: add wide_pointer_add_load_store_and_gep_base_widen_when_exact_and_refuse_when_inexact
  covering both exact pointer-Add + Load/Store/GEP-base widening and the
  IVW-RANGE-1 exposed-latch refusal.
- narrow_copy_fold_tests: add upper32_zero_promotes_32bit_copy_and_base_read_rewrites_copy_site
  covering upper32_zero_at 32->64 copy promotion and copy-site collapse when
  the base register is read before the copy.
- relay_and_lea: extend rmw_window_tests to cover the 2-RMW window (MAX_RMWS = 2)
  and destination-family-read refusal.

Audit Census Ratchet & Cleanup
- Revert the non-behavioural function extraction in load_op_fuse.rs while
  unifying accumulator binary/divrem arms in x86/codegen/alu.rs and simplifying
  preference selection in regalloc.rs, ratcheting fns_over_1000 (28 -> 27),
  holding fns_over_300 at 230, and reducing panic_sites (848 -> 834).
